'''''The Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes''''' is an American [[superhero fiction|superhero]] [[animated series]] produced by [[Marvel Animation]] in cooperation with [[Film Roman]] based on the [[Marvel Comics]] [[Avengers (comics)|superhero team]]. The first season debuted on [[Disney XD]] on September 22, 2010. The second season was one of the inaugural shows of the Marvel Universe programming block alongside ''[[Ultimate Spider-Man (TV series)|Ultimate Spider-Man]]''.<ref name="XDApril1"/> The series originally features a team based on the roster for the original Avengers, consisting of [[Iron Man]], the [[Hulk]], [[Thor (Marvel Comics)|Thor]], [[Hank Pym|Ant-Man]], and [[Wasp (character)|Wasp]]. The team is later joined by [[Captain America]], [[Black Panther (character)|Black Panther]], and [[Hawkeye (Clint Barton)|Hawkeye]] in the first season, and [[Carol Danvers|Ms. Marvel]] and [[Vision (Marvel Comics)|Vision]] in the second.

In terms of overall tone and style, the series is based on the original stories by [[Stan Lee]] and [[Jack Kirby]]. The series also uses material from all eras of the comic's run as well as other sources, such as the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]].<ref name="comicscontinuum.com">{{cite web|url=http://www.comicscontinuum.com/stories/1004/18/marvelanimation.htm|title=C2E2: Marvel Animation|publisher=comicscontinuum.com|date=April 18, 2010|access-date=August 13, 2010|archive-date=April 18, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210418110702/http://www.comicscontinuum.com/stories/1004/18/marvelanimation.htm|url-status=dead}}</ref>

==Synopsis==
[[File:Breakout (The Avengers- Earth's Mightiest Heroes).jpg|thumb|The original Avengers. From left to right: Ant-Man / Giant-Man, Iron Man, the Hulk, Wasp, and Thor|left]]

===Season one===
Following a mass [[prison breakout]] at the [[Vault (Marvel Comics)|Vault]], the [[Cube (comics)|Cube]], the [[Big House (comics)|Big House]], and the [[Raft (comics)|Raft]], Earth's mightiest heroes unite to form the [[Avengers (comics)|Avengers]], a team comprising [[Iron Man]], [[Captain America]], [[Thor (Marvel Comics)|Thor]], the [[Hulk]], [[Hank Pym|Ant-Man]], [[Wasp (character)|Wasp]], [[Black Panther (character)|Black Panther]], and [[Hawkeye (Clint Barton)|Hawkeye]].<ref name="IGN">{{cite web |last=Iverson |first=Dan |date=July 25, 2010 |title=SDCC 10: The Avengers Assemble On The Small Screen |url=http://tv.ign.com/articles/110/1108401p1.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100727105914/http://tv.ign.com/articles/110/1108401p1.html |archive-date=July 27, 2010 |access-date=August 13, 2010 |publisher=IGN}}</ref> The Avengers battle various supervillains including [[Heinrich Zemo|Baron Zemo]], the [[Leader (character)|Leader]], [[Kang the Conqueror]], and [[Ultron]], as well as the criminal organizations [[Hydra (comics)|Hydra]] and [[Advanced Idea Mechanics|A.I.M.]] It is ultimately revealed that [[Loki (Marvel Comics)|Loki]] orchestrated the breakout and had the [[Enchantress (Marvel Comics)|Enchantress]] form the [[Masters of Evil]] to distract the Avengers as part of his scheme to conquer the nine realms, including [[Asgard (comics)|Asgard]].

=== Season two ===
Following Loki's defeat, the Avengers are joined by [[Carol Danvers|Ms. Marvel]] and the [[Vision (Marvel Comics)|Vision]] as they hunt down the remnants of the Masters of Evil and face new enemies including [[Doctor Doom]], the [[Thunderbolt Ross|Red Hulk]], and the [[Red Skull]], as well as alien threats such as the [[Skrull]]s, the [[Kree]], and [[Galactus]]. The season alludes to a developing storyline in which [[Surtur (character)|Surtur]] escapes [[Muspelheim]] and gathers strength to oppose the Avengers as a prelude to [[Ragnarök]].

Numerous other Marvel Comics characters make guest appearances, such as [[Spider-Man]], [[Wolverine (character)|Wolverine]], Ant-Man ([[Scott Lang]]), the [[Heroes for Hire]], the [[Guardians of the Galaxy (2008 team)|Guardians of the Galaxy]], [[Daisy Johnson]] (Quake), [[Beta Ray Bill]], [[Falcon (comics)|Falcon]], and [[Bucky Barnes|Winter Soldier]].

